<h1>SEO/AEO/GEO Optimization Case Study</h1>
<p>This project tests how a public B2B SaaS site can be evaluated for both traditional search and AI-mediated discovery. It is an independent analysis, not client work.</p>
<h2>Research question</h2><p>Which page, entity and evidence signals make a brand easier to retrieve, summarize, cite and compare — and where does a conventional SEO audit fail to capture those signals?</p>
<h2>Method</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>1 · Baseline</h3><p>Map target pages, category language, entities, technical discoverability and observable search/AI presence.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>2 · Query fan-out</h3><p>Build prompt families for category discovery, alternatives, comparisons, capabilities, pricing and buyer-stage questions.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>3 · Retrieval audit</h3><p>Evaluate answerability, citation-ready evidence, information architecture, structured data and source consistency.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>4 · Intervention design</h3><p>Produce concrete page restructures and content recommendations. Proposed changes remain distinct from observed results.</p></article></div>
<h2>Evidence standard</h2><p>Observed public evidence, interpretation and proposed intervention are reported separately. No traffic, ranking, citation or revenue improvement is claimed unless it can be measured after an intervention.</p>
<h2>Benchmark dimensions</h2><p>AI visibility is decomposed into brand mention coverage, citation coverage, recommendation inclusion, source patterns and consistency across prompt families rather than collapsed into one opaque score.</p>
</Base>